# Interface rules

Read `DESIGN.md` before changing the shell, tokens or motion. The token block in
`app/src/styles.css` is the only place raw colours belong.

- One job per page. The rail is the table of contents; the inspector always
  carries the current session, primary action, progress and queue.
- Use the existing tokens and component classes (`.card`, `.panel`, `.chip`,
  `.pill`, `.title`, `.progress`, `.mode`, `.field`, `.mini`). Do not invent a
  parallel scale.
- Every interactive control needs hover, active, `:focus-visible` and disabled
  states. Icon-only controls need an `aria-label`.
- Animate transform and opacity only. Progress width is the single exception.
  Add a reduced-motion path for anything new.
- Copy is short and specific. No em or en dashes, no promises the code does not
  keep.
- Preview with `cd app && npm run dev:mock` and screenshot 1440x900 and
  1000x760 layouts. `npm run build` must pass before committing.
